test/inductor/test_aot_inductor_package.py::TestAOTInductorPackageCpp_cuda::test_compile_with_exporter

I looked at this, and it seems that the meta kernel returns torch.empty_like(input) which copies the input dtype (float32) instead of using the dtype  parameter. This accidentally bypasses the FakeTensor is_quantized check letting quantized ops reach CPP codegen where aoti_torch_dtype_quint8 doesn't exist. 

If we fix the meta kernel to return the right dtype, it would restore the graph break. Adding the full support i.e, in fake tensors, and codegen and then actual c++ implementation is an involved fix (it seems). 

